            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation of common breast complaints in primary care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8-15</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000524661.93974.e8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Discovery of a breast mass, nipple discharge, or breast pain is a common, anxiety-producing occurrence for many women. Although most irregularities are benign, every woman presenting with a breast complaint should be evaluated to exclude or establish a diagnosis of cancer. The patient visit to the provider for a breast complaint can also present an opportunity for the NP to address and update any needed breast screenings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
